::SECTION_30_DIRECTX12_AND_GPU_SYNCHRONIZATION::
@FAULT_NODE [ERR-DX12-001] {
    DOMAIN          : "DirectX 12 Command Allocators, Fences & Resource State Barriers (ID3D12GraphicsCommandList)"
    PHENOMENON      : "`DXGI_ERROR_DEVICE_REMOVED` (0x887A0005), command allocator reset race conditions, or GPU page faults"
    ROOT_CAUSE      : "Calling `ID3D12CommandAllocator::Reset()` while the GPU command queue is still executing commands from that allocator, or transitioning resources across incompatible states."
    INVARIANT_RULE  : "Track per-frame `ID3D12Fence` values, wait on `GetCompletedValue() < frameFenceValue` via `SetEventOnCompletion` before resetting allocators, and validate `D3D12_RESOURCE_BARRIER` before/after state transitions."
}

@FAULT_NODE [ERR-DX12-002] {
    DOMAIN          : "Descriptor Heap Bounds & Root Signature Slot Alignment"
    PHENOMENON      : "Silent rendering corruption or `D3D12 ERROR` debug layer faults on CBV/SRV/UAV bindings"
    ROOT_CAUSE      : "Exceeding `NumDescriptors` capacity when incrementing `CD3DX12_CPU_DESCRIPTOR_HANDLE` offsets or binding root parameter indices out of order."
    INVARIANT_RULE  : "Query `GetDescriptorHandleIncrementSize` per heap type at init, enforce hard slot capacity bounds checks, and match root signature parameter indices strictly to HLSL `register()` declarations."
}

::SECTION_31_REGISTRY_WRAPPERS_AND_NATIVE_DEPLOYMENT::
@FAULT_NODE [ERR-REG-001] {
    DOMAIN          : "Pure WinAPI / reg.exe Installer Wrappers & File Association Deployment"
    PHENOMENON      : "`ERROR_ACCESS_DENIED` (Exit Code 1), partial HKCU/HKLM split registrations, or unrefreshed Explorer shell icons"
    ROOT_CAUSE      : "Writing to `HKLM` without checking elevated token privileges, omitting `/reg:64` on 64-bit systems, or failing to notify Windows Explorer after `.AVIS` / `.cyborg` association writes."
    INVARIANT_RULE  : "Default per-user associations to `HKCU\\Software\\Classes`, pass explicit `/reg:64 /f` flags to `reg.exe`, and broadcast `SHChangeNotify(SHCNE_ASSOCCHANGED, SHCNF_IDLIST, NULL, NULL)` upon completion."
}

::SECTION_32_WINDOW_PRESENTATION_AND_FLICKER_ELIMINATION::
@FAULT_NODE [ERR-VSYNC-001] {
    DOMAIN          : "Win32 Window Class Background Erasure & DXGI Flip-Model Swap Chains"
    PHENOMENON      : "Severe visual flashing/flickering during window resize or high-frequency frame updates"
    ROOT_CAUSE      : "Leaving a non-null `hbrBackground` on `WNDCLASSEXW` (causing GDI `WM_ERASEBKGND` white/black flashes before GPU present) or using legacy `DXGI_SWAP_EFFECT_DISCARD`."
    INVARIANT_RULE  : "Set `wc.hbrBackground = NULL`, intercept `WM_ERASEBKGND` returning `1`, and configure swap chains with `DXGI_SWAP_EFFECT_FLIP_DISCARD` and explicit `Present(1, 0)` VSync cadence."
}

::MASTER_VERIFICATION_GATE::
@GATE_CHECK_F10 {
    32. DX12_FENCE_SYNC    : Gate `CommandAllocator::Reset()` behind completed `ID3D12Fence` signals and validate resource barrier state transitions.
    33. REG64_SHELL_NOTIFY : Scope user associations to `HKCU\\Software\\Classes`, enforce `/reg:64 /f`, and emit `SHChangeNotify(SHCNE_ASSOCCHANGED, ...)`.
    34. ZERO_ERASE_PRESENT : Suppress GDI `WM_ERASEBKGND` erasure (`hbrBackground = NULL`) and use `DXGI_SWAP_EFFECT_FLIP_DISCARD`.
}
::AVIS_MANIFEST_END::
